{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. ___, I’m Dr. ___. I understand your line came out earlier today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it just fell out. I didn’t pull it or anything. I was worried because I haven’t had my remodulin in over three hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. That’s why we restarted your remodulin through a temporary IV in your arm. You’re getting it now, so you’re not going without."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I hate going without it. Last time I did, I felt short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s why we need to replace your tunneled line quickly. The team is scheduling it for tonight. It’ll go back into your neck vein and end in your heart, just like before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it be safe? My platelets are low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked that. Your platelet count is low due to your liver disease, and the blood bank says you don’t respond well to transfusions. So we’ll proceed carefully without one, since you’ve had procedures before without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, as long as it’s safe. And my back pain—can I still take my usual pain meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2178-08-23 19:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep your MS Contin and Dilaudid for breakthrough pain. The imaging shows your old compression fractures are stable, so we’ll manage it the same way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2178-08-23 21:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure is done. We placed the new tunneled line through your right internal jugular vein. The tip is in the right atrium, and it’s working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2178-08-23 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Is it safe to use right away?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2178-08-23 21:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We confirmed it flushes easily and draws blood. The priming volume is only 1 mL, so it’s efficient. You’ll go back to your home remodulin dose tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2178-08-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs are stable—same as before. No signs of infection. We did a chest X-ray after the procedure to make sure there was no pneumothorax."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2178-08-24 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had some shortness of breath afterward. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2178-08-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray showed some patchy opacities in your lungs, likely from your chronic lung disease. No pneumonia or fluid. Your oxygen levels are good at 93% on room air, so we think it’s stable portopulmonary syndrome."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’ll discharge you today. You’ve already infused your home remodulin dose through the new line without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I manage it myself at home. No nurse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and you’re confident doing it. Just keep all your meds going—sildenafil, spironolactone, rifaximin, and the testosterone patch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the diuretics for my belly swelling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, torsemide and spironolactone continue. Watch your weight—call if you gain more than three pounds in a day. And follow up with transplant clinic as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the dressing dry for 48 hours. After that, you can shower. Watch for redness, swelling, or fever—call us if those happen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my back pain? It’s still there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep your gabapentin and narcotics. The fractures are stable, so it’s chronic pain. We’ll address it at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel better knowing the line is back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2178-08-24 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready. You can go home in a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2178-08-24 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your scrotal swelling has increased a bit. It’s likely from fluid due to cirrhosis. Keep taking your diuretics and monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2178-08-24 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch it. Thanks for everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2178-08-23 19:18:00",
    "admission_end": "2178-08-24 19:17:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted after his tunneled central line spontaneously displaced, interrupting his continuous remodulin infusion for portopulmonary hypertension. He was stabilized with a peripheral IV remodulin infusion and underwent urgent placement of a new right internal jugular tunneled catheter, which was successfully implanted with the tip in the right atrium. He tolerated the procedure well without complications. His chronic conditions, including cirrhosis, ascites, thrombocytopenia, and vertebral compression fractures, remained stable. He resumed his home remodulin dose through the new line and was discharged home the following day with instructions to monitor weight, manage his line, and follow up with transplant clinic. No new infections or procedural complications occurred.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications due to other vascular device, implant, and graft",
      "Surgical operation with implant of artificial internal device causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Other chronic pulmonary heart diseases",
      "Unspecified viral hepatitis C without hepatic coma",
      "Cirrhosis of liver without mention of alcohol",
      "Other testicular hypofunction",
      "Thrombocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Other pancytopenia",
      "Unspecified protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Pathologic fracture of vertebrae",
      "Osteoporosis, unspecified",
      "Hepatopulmonary syndrome"
    ]
  }
}
